From: Tensor G1 PRoot GPU experiment
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: link external-memory sources into X11 WSI

The X11 DMA-BUF image factory references the external-memory extension and
backing implementation, but the X11 source list does not compile them. Add the
two required sources to the shared WSI layer build.

---
 CMakeLists.txt | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 1679c18..cd5fb31 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -305,7 +305,9 @@ if(BUILD_WSI_X11)
       wsi/x11/surface.cpp
       wsi/x11/swapchain.cpp
       wsi/x11/shm_presenter.cpp
-      wsi/x11/dri3_presenter.cpp)
+      wsi/x11/dri3_presenter.cpp
+      wsi/extensions/external_memory_extension.cpp
+      wsi/image_backing_memory_external.cpp)
 
    pkg_check_modules(LIBDRM REQUIRED libdrm)
 
-- 
2.50.1
